Subject: Set the desktop file name before the welcome wizard is shown

main_window sets org.octave.Octave in its constructor, after the first-run
welcome wizard has taken the executable's name, octave-gui, as its Wayland app
id. Set it when the application object is made.

--- a/libgui/src/octave-qobject.cc
+++ b/libgui/src/octave-qobject.cc
@@ -229,6 +229,10 @@
   // Force left-to-right alignment (see bug #46204)
   m_qapplication->setLayoutDirection (Qt::LeftToRight);
 
+  // The Wayland app id of every window, the welcome wizard included: set
+  // before the first one is created.
+  QGuiApplication::setDesktopFileName ("org.octave.Octave");
+
   // Make sure Qt picks a full OpenGL context (including deprecated
   // functions, see bug #67974)
 #if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(5, 4, 0)
